"hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2766,"Abdul Jabbar ibn Al-Ala narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Urwah, who said: I recited in the presence of Aisha, ""Indeed, As-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah"" (Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 158). I said: I do not see anything wrong upon one who does not perform tawaf between them. She said: What an evil thing you have said, O son of my sister! It was only those who dedicated themselves to Manat, the idol which was at Al-Mushallal, who used to perform tawaf between As-Safa and Al-Marwah. When Islam came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, our tawaf between these two hills was a practice of the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah). She said: Then this was revealed: ""Indeed, As-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah."" She said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf between them, and it became an established practice (Sunnah).

And someone other than her said: Allah said: ""So whoever volunteers good..."" Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ volunteered and performed tawaf.

Az-Zuhri said: I narrated this to Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman, and he said: This is indeed knowledge. I have heard men of knowledge"
2767,"Narrated to us by Isa ibn Ibrahim, who said: Narrated to us by Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aisha (RA) informed him: Before the Ansar embraced Islam, and before Ghassan did, they used to invoke (make talbiyah for) Manat. Consequently, they felt religious scruple (was hesitant) to perform Tawaf between As-Safa and Al-Marwah. This was their established custom in those days"
2768,"**
Narrated to us Bakr ibn Khālid, on the authority of ʿĀṣim, on the authority of Anas ibn Mālik (RA), who said:
The Ansār used to dislike performing the Tawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah until the verse was revealed:
*""Indeed, aṣ-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.""*
[Qur'an 2:158]

Salm ibn Junādah (RA) added:
So they began to perform the Tawāf between them."
